        "location": "engine/runtime/labdrian-runtime-parity-plugin.mjs:483-488",
        "claim": "The engine's per-prompt answer is now written into the user's prompt text, which OpenCode stores as the message. Before, it was transient system context that lasted only until the next prompt. Now each prompt's context and warning is persisted in the conversation history, shown in the transcript and possibly used for the session title, and it keeps costing tokens in every later turn. The diff does not show whether OpenCode re-runs the prompt hook on retries or resubmits, which would append the block twice. The change trades the cache problem for history growth and a changed user-visible message.",
